A three-dimensional rotor system with quantized energy (having two rotational degrees of freedom, no translational motion) obeys Boltzmann statistics. Calculate the free energy for each rotor at high temperatures. The energy of the rotor is

$$
\varepsilon_{j}=j(j+1) \hbar^{2} / 2 I=A j(j+1)
$$

where $I$ is the moment of inertia of the rotor, the rotational quantum number $j=0,1,2, \cdots$, Planck's constant $\hbar=1.055 \times 10^{-34} \mathrm{~J} \cdot \mathrm{~s}$, and $A=\hbar^{2} / 2 I$. The degeneracy of the energy level $\varepsilon_{j}$ is given by $g_{j}=2 j+1$. The partition function of the rotor is

